    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Change\n\nThe requirement: after an owner's telephone is normalized to canonical E.164, validate its **national-number length against the country code** \u2014 `+61` needs 9 national digits, `+1` needs 10 \u2014 and reject with **400** when wrong.\n\n**`TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 added a per-country length table and a validation method, keeping all telephone logic in the one place already responsible for it:\n\n```java\nprivate static final Map<String, Integer> NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS = Map.of(\"61\", 9, \"1\", 10);\n\npublic boolean hasValidNationalNumberLength(String e164Telephone) {\n    if (e164Telephone == null || !e164Telephone.startsWith(\"+\")) {\n        return false;\n    }\n    String digits = e164Telephone.substring(1);\n    for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> entry : NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS.entrySet()) {\n        String countryCode = entry.getKey();\n        if (digits.startsWith(countryCode)) {\n            return digits.length() - countryCode.length() == entry.getValue();\n        }\n    }\n    return true;   // no pinned length for this country code\n}\n```\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 invoked it right after the existing normalize/null check in `addOwner`, returning `400 BAD_REQUEST` on a mismatch:\n\n```java\nif (!telephoneNormalizer.hasValidNationalNumberLength(telephone)) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n}\n```\n\n## Notes on correctness\n- The two country-code prefixes (`61` \u2192 `+6\u2026`, `1` \u2192 `+1\u2026`) are mutually exclusive at the leading digit, so map iteration order is irrelevant.\n- The check runs only on the incoming request. The `+61` numbers created by tests via `uniqueTelephone()` normalize to 9 national digits and stay valid; seed-data numbers are only ever passed through `normalize()` for duplicate comparison, never through this validator.\n- Country codes without a pinned length fall through to `true`, preserving the generic 8\u201315 digit E.164 rule already enforced by `normalize()`.\n\nAll tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
